# ---- HOST-NATIVE STATION (native from day one — samcoupe wave, 2026-09-08) ----
# MAME 0.289's samcoupe runs ON THE HOST — same engine as apple2e/mpf2,
# drawshm frames, ctlsock keys through the generated keymap, sound -> SDL
# disk -> FIFO with the daemon as clock. Launcher: shared
# stations/mame-native/x11-runtime.sh; reset = relaunch restoring the golden
# savestate (src/mame/samcoupe/samcoupe.cpp (MACHINE_SUPPORTS_SAVE)).
SH_RESET_MODE=relaunch
SH_FIXTURE_DESC=SAM Coupé "KERNEL HIVE - SAM COUPE" boot menu (5 entries: 1 Manic Miner, 2 Mr Pac, 3 Splat!, 4 The Secretary, B SAM BASIC) baked into the golden savestate so a visitor never sees the MGT copyright banner or the BOOT keystroke -- MEASURED 2026-09-08 on a sandbox rig: cold boot -> banner 0 s (immediate), banner-dismiss Enter + typed BOOT+Enter -> menu settled 9.0 s total from process start, SAVEST at the menu 13 ms / 11871 bytes, fresh relaunch with -state golden -> menu settled 4.7 s and PIL-diff bbox None against the baked menu frame (pixel-identical). HOST-NATIVE drawshm frames, ctlsock keys through the generated keymap. Keyboard verdict: `1` (Manic Miner) verified end-to-end at the fleet 40/40 ms pacing -- key lands, disk load reaches the title screen ("Game One / The story so far...") with no dropped/duplicated characters. `B` (SAM BASIC) is NOT fully verified on the real ctlsock KEY path: CLS runs (menu text clears) but the guest lands in the BASIC program-EDIT view (an arrow cursor on program line 10), not the clean "0 OK" prompt the media stream saw from its Lua -autoboot_command harness; typing further characters there edits the listed line rather than entering a new command, and produced a `12 Missing DEF PROC` parse error once submitted. OPEN item for a follow-up stream: find the extra key (ESC/BREAK, or a differently-timed Enter) that clears the edit view to a bare `0 OK` prompt on the real input path before calling `B`/BASIC access verified.
MAME_NATIVE_BIN=/data/vms/streamhost/assets/samcoupe/mame-native/samcoupe
MAME_NATIVE_DRIVER=samcoupe
MAME_NATIVE_ROMS=/data/vms/streamhost/assets/samcoupe/mame-native/roms
MAME_NATIVE_GEOM=1024x768
MAME_NATIVE_SKIP_WARNINGS=0
# Golden stream, 2026-09-08: SAVEST at the menu (13 ms, 11871 bytes) restores
# via a fresh relaunch with -state golden pixel-identical to the baked frame
# (PIL diff bbox None) -- decision, not a default: keep =1.
MAME_NATIVE_CHECKPOINT=1
# Device set CONFIRMED on this 0.289 build (2026-09-08, native stream):
# -listslots samcoupe shows drive1/drive2 both default to slot option
# "floppy" (SAM Coupé Internal Floppy, media flop1/flop2); set explicitly so
# a MAME default change can never silently drop it. No mouseport option is
# attached -- keyboard-only exhibit (stream.pointer.transport stays "none").
# -flop1 points at the media stream's composed disk; on a cold boot it does
# NOT auto-boot -- Enter (dismiss the copyright screen to SAM BASIC) then
# BOOT<Enter> is needed to reach "KERNEL HIVE - SAM COUPE". Golden stream
# decision (2026-09-08): the golden savestate is captured WITH THE MENU
# ALREADY UP (see MAME_NATIVE_CHECKPOINT above), so the fleet's relaunch
# restore skips this keying entirely -- no launch-arg automation is needed.
# A cold boot (MAME_NATIVE_CHECKPOINT=0, or the very first boot before a
# golden exists) would still need it keyed, which is not implemented here.
MAME_NATIVE_ARGS=-drive1 floppy -drive2 floppy -flop1 /data/vms/streamhost/assets/samcoupe/media/hive.mgt
SH_MAMECTL_SOCK=/data/vms/streamhost/stations/samcoupe/ctl.sock
SH_MAMESOCK_KEYMAP=/data/vms/streamhost/stations/samcoupe/samcoupe.keymap
SH_AUDIO_SOURCE=fifo
SH_AUDIO_FIFO=/data/vms/streamhost/stations/samcoupe/audio.fifo

SH_IDLE_PAUSE_SECS=60
SH_IDLE_PAUSE_PIDFILE=/data/vms/streamhost/stations/samcoupe/mame.pid
SH_IDLE_PAUSE_PROC_MATCH=assets/samcoupe/mame-native
MAME_NATIVE_STANDBY_DELAY_S=8

# Fleet floor for MAME keyboard stations (playbook §0): measure only if
# characters drop. A CPU-scanned matrix may need MAME_CTL_KEY_EXCL=1.
SH_KEY_MIN_HOLD_MS=40
SH_KEY_MIN_GAP_MS=40
